# `$isAsBorn(object, maker)`: THE DOOR ASKED OF AN OBJECT THAT A LITERAL MADE: the object has the layout of the one object literal of `maker`, each of its names lies in its slot, nothing was added, it is not frozen, sealed or closed,
# and above it stands what stood there at its birth. The layout is named by binding: the function whose one literal it is. The walk stamps the operation of `$isPlainInstanceOf` with that layout; a literal has no guards of a class.
# Behind the yes a read of one of the names is a read of a slot. A maker with two literals names no layout: the question is left as written and answers false.
# The answer says what the object is, not who made it: SAMENAMES: a literal of run-time code with the same names is given the same layout by the interpreter (planObjectLiteral) and gets a yes: a read of its names runs no code either.
